# The pages of loom.luciaos.com, in order.
#
# One row per page: SLUG | NAV LABEL | TITLE | DESCRIPTION.  The first
# row is the front page and its slug is empty, so it is written to
# `out/index.html`; every other row becomes `out/SLUG/index.html`.
#
# The order here is the order of the tabs in the bar and the order the
# Previous/Next links walk, so adding a page is one row and a file
# under `content/`.  Nothing else lists the pages.

	Overview	loom	The environment that runs compiled Luce: a shell, a runner, an editor, and the host boundary programs reach the world through.
running	Running	Running programs	How loom starts a program: one dlopen for a .lc, compile-and-cache for a .luc, artifacts refused by name, and the exit status a script reads afterwards.
shell	Shell	The shell	loom's interactive line shell — its five commands, bare program paths, colour, and what a piped script gets that a person at a prompt does not.
editor	Editor	The editor	loom edit: a full-screen editor with Luce syntax highlighting, written in Luce, carried inside the loom binary.
host	Host	The host	Every effect a Luce program can have is a service loom hands it. The whole surface, the gate that governs it, and why a missing service refuses rather than guesses.
direction	Direction	Where loom is going	What v1 wanted, what v2 kept and dropped, and the honest shape of loom's growth. Direction, not documentation of anything built.
